codex
The new receiver check can produce a false RED for valid Rust method receiver syntax, which undermines the conformance gate's stated goal of accepting legal receiver spellings while blocking receiver-less functions.

Review comment:

- [P2] Allow explicit `self:` receivers — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/orch-0.8.20-s30/scripts/check-c1-conformance.sh:740-740
  If `configure_projections` is rewritten with Rust's explicit receiver syntax, e.g. `self: &Self`, it remains an instance method and existing `engine.configure_projections(..)` call sites still compile, but this regex only accepts shorthand forms like `&self`/`mut self`. That would make the conformance gate fail on a valid method shape despite the seam contract still being preserved.
